language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_067_quasigroup_completion: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ An order N quasigroup is a Latin square of size N: an N x N multiplication table in which each value from 1 to N occurs exactly once in every row and every column. Complete a partially filled quasigroup, in which 0 marks an empty cell, to a full quasigroup that keeps every filled value.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_067_quasigroup_completion.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_067_quasigroup_completion.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_067_quasigroup_completion_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_067_quasigroup_completion.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_067_quasigroup_completion_1.param -run-solver

$ N: the order of the quasigroup (the side of the square)
given N : int(1..)
$ start[i,j]: the value of the starting square in row i, column j (indices 1-based, so the data's index 0 is 1); 0 marks an empty cell
given start : matrix indexed by [int(1..N), int(1..N)] of int(0..N)

$ puzzle[i,j]: the completed value in row i, column j (indices 1-based), a value from 1 to N
find puzzle : matrix indexed by [int(1..N), int(1..N)] of int(1..N)

branching on [puzzle]
such that
$ every row contains each value from 1 to N exactly once
forAll i : int(1..N) . allDiff(puzzle[i,..]),
$ every column contains each value from 1 to N exactly once
forAll j : int(1..N) . allDiff(puzzle[..,j]),
$ every filled cell of the starting square keeps its given value (an empty cell, 0, is unconstrained)
forAll i : int(1..N) . forAll j : int(1..N) . (start[i,j] = 0 \/ puzzle[i,j] = start[i,j])
